<title>USA: Florida to sell $168 mln bonds for agency. [CORRECTED 19:44 GMT]</title>
<headline>Florida to sell $168 mln bonds for agency. [CORRECTED 19:44 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida said it plans to sell $168 million senior lien refunding series 1997 full faith and credit bonds for the Jacksonville Transportation Authority.</p>
<p>(Corrects headline and text to make clear that Florida state, not the authority, is the issuer.)</p>
<p>The bonds will be sold by competitive bid on 20 hours notice, the state said.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
